# report-export Docker build-context exclusions (docs/design.md §4.7.2).
#
# NAMING NOTE (deviation from an earlier design draft's directory tree, which
# lists this file as `docker/.dockerignore`): BuildKit only honours a
# plain `.dockerignore` when it sits in the CONTEXT ROOT (report-export/,
# per the documented `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` invocation),
# never next to a Dockerfile that lives in a subdirectory -- a
# `docker/.dockerignore` file is silently never read and would exclude
# nothing. The correct BuildKit convention for a non-root Dockerfile is
# `<dockerfile-basename>.dockerignore`, co-located with that Dockerfile
# -- i.e. exactly this file. Verified empirically against this
# project's own `docker build -t report-export:1.0.0 -f docker/Dockerfile .`
# invocation before adopting this name. This is the single ignore file
# for this build; there is no second, non-functional `.dockerignore`
# copy left behind to drift out of sync with it.
#
# Rationale for the exclusions below: keep the build context small and
# keep dev-only, runtime-generated, or already-baselined-elsewhere
# content out of the image entirely. Nothing here is read by any COPY
# in docker/Dockerfile -- every COPY instruction names its sources
# explicitly, so these patterns are a build-context-size / hygiene
# control, not a correctness dependency.

# Input template + e2e fixture baseline (2.3MB xlsx + source-log.csv):
# already checked in as a traceable baseline (design.md §4.7.7); the
# runtime image never reads it (only tests/tools do).
template/

# Runtime-generated, machine-owned, per-run state (design.md §3.5, §4.7.7)
# -- never baked into an image; always host bind-mounted (design.md
# §4.7.5). Matches the top-level .gitignore (both the top-level and the
# REQ2-relocated docker/{inbox,state,output}/ runtime dirs -- these
# patterns are unanchored, so they already match at any depth, but the
# docker/ paths are listed explicitly too for readability).
state/
output/
inbox/
docker/inbox/
docker/state/
docker/output/

# Committed REQ4 demo fixtures (docker/example/**, design.md §4.7.7) --
# input, docs and tools/tests-driven fixtures, never read by any COPY
# in this Dockerfile; keep the build context small.
docker/example/

# Dev-only: tests, docs, and the one-off HOSP-table export tool never
# ship in the runtime image (design.md §3.3, §4.7.1, §4.7.2).
tests/
docs/
tools/

# VCS and Docker's own convenience files.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Python / tooling litter (mirrors the top-level .gitignore).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
